<title>POLAND: ESPEBEPE EXTENDS SURGE ON DEBT-DEAL HOPES.</title>
<headline>ESPEBEPE EXTENDS SURGE ON DEBT-DEAL HOPES.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish debt-ridden construction firm Espebepe extended Tuesday's surge, rising 9.1 percent, to 5.4 zlotys on hopes that the firm would convince its creditors to accept its new restructuring programme, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Some investors speculate on hopes that Espebepe would be rescued from bankruptcy, but the risk of such investment is still extremely high,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday Espebepe said it had worked out a new debt restructuring programme, envisaging a new issue and said the scheme had already been accepted by its shareholders.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
